  "boundaries": [
    "Exact-original test-only controls reproduce recoverable-ancestor eviction by obsolete forward work and needless retirement by an obsolete queued rewind. Held read access plus fair-lock writer queuing identifies the actual storage await.",
    "The forward mechanism uses reduced tracker depths 3 and 8. Production depth is 8192; larger-gap consequences are source composition, not production-sized or live-chain observation.",
    "Reorg controls retain all physical rows. The confirmed effect is unnecessary rewind/refetch and availability loss, not permanent data loss.",
    "Materialized CL replacement fixtures isolate consumer admission. They do not establish acceptance of signed network consensus messages.",
    "Publication compares full captured anchor and the existing selected-lineage readiness predicate. Compatible extensions and unrelated metadata remain accepted, and higher unmaterialized selected-head behavior is retained without claiming ancestry proof.",
    "Synchronous admission linearizes against in-memory selection. It does not promise future finality or atomic cross-file consensus/execution durability.",
    "Full reorg scan and pending-write checkpoint remain outside CL. Intent publication still serializes catalog and performs durability I/O; no constant-time or hard-latency bound is claimed.",
    "A single prospective retained-header snapshot replaces the original persistence snapshot. Successful append hashes only new headers; no full-window restore in ordinary ingestion. No throughput benchmark is claimed.",
    "Dropped active reorg handles preserve required recovery with no Drop I/O; no-op and invalid requests retain existing semantics. Existing journal/format and failpoint order are unchanged.",
    "Historical ancestry, empty/genesis progress, ordered outcomes and queue ownership have a scoped source-and-existing-regression disposition; no global RSS/byte bound is inferred.",
    "No broad benchmark, live sync, remote host, production-data, physical-volume, deployment, dependency or authoritative format change.",
    "Broader offline audit and automatic repair remain open; live sync and staging soak follow offline completion."
  ]
